# conveyor.fmat — UV scroll, as a material.
#
# This was `uv_scroll:` on an entity model attachment — a tank's track belt —
# and it was the only thing in the engine that had it. A wall could not scroll.
#
# A material's scroll is a pure function of the clock rather than a per-surface
# counter, because the same document is worn by every belt in the level and one
# of them cannot be allowed to advance a counter the others share. So every
# surface wearing this scrolls in step, which is what a row of conveyors wants.
# A surface with its OWN uv_scroll still drifts independently, and the two add.
kind: surface
doc: A belt running along +V. Put it on the top face of the run.
effects:
  - effect: uv_scroll
    rate: [0, 0.6]
